s/by-nc/3.0/"/></ore:Aggregation><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/provider/9200211/en_list_one_bcuf_L0037"><dc:coverage>Dijon</dc:coverage><dc:creator>Boethius, Anicius Manlius Severinus</dc:creator><dc:date>1447</dc:date><dc:description>Few works of antiquity had as profound an influence on the Middle Ages as did Boethius’ De Consolatione Philosophiae. This exemplar contains valuable information which allows it to be placed in an interesting historical context. The Fribourg cleric Pierre Guillomin finished copying the manuscript on Christmas Eve 1447 in Dijon. The colophon, which states these details, also names the recipient of the manuscript, Jacques Trompettaz († 1503), a compatriot of the copyist. The latter was careful to include in several passages of the text, in addition to his own name and that of the addressee, the names of two more Fribourg friends, Claude de Gruyère and Jacques Sutz, Monk at Hauterive.</dc:description><dc:format>147 ff., 22 x 15 cm</dc:format><dc:identifier>doi:10.5076/e-codices-bcuf-L0037</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/bcuf/L0037</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>Fribourg/Freiburg, Bibliothèque cantonale et universitaire/Kantons- und Universitätsbibliothek, Ms. L 37</dc:identifier><dc:publisher>e-codices - Virtual Manuscript Library of Switzerland</dc:publisher><dc:language>Latin</dc:language><dc:relation>Jurot Romain, Catalogue des manuscrits médiévaux de la Bibliothèque cantonale et universitaire de Fribourg, Dietikon-Zürich 2006, p. 102-103.</dc:relation><dc:rights>e-codices / Fribourg/Freiburg, Bibliothèque cantonale et universitaire/Kantons- und Universitätsbibliothek (cf. http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/about/terms)</dc:rights><dc:source rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/bcuf/L0037"></dc:source><dc:title>Fribourg/Freiburg, Bibliothèque cantonale et universitaire/Kantons- und Universitätsbibliothek, Ms. L 37 : Boetius</dc:title><dc:type>Manuscript</dc: